<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vlie</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vlie is a tidal channel between the West Frisian islands of Vlieland and Terschelling in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, linking the Wadden Sea with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was the outlet of waters draining the inland lake that grew into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zuiderzee">Zuiderzee</a>, and it marked a boundary between Holland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frisia">Frisia</a>. In 1666 an English fleet burned a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> merchant fleet there, an attack known as Holmes's Bonfire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vlie.jpg" alt="Vlie" width="320" height="467" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MWAK · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vlie9.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
